# Weakens H's HandOffBound in this module's environment from the close's side: the
# close records heads below the allocator head, so a foreign record of the window
# lies at or above them. The core replays only to the recorded heads, and its live
# advance passes the record.
MODULE: ReadPositionHonestAssumeCloseHeadUnderstated
TARGET: ReadPositionHonest
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a close records any heads at or below the allocator head
PERTURBS: Close

--- FIND
    /\ hoOpen' = FALSE
    /\ hoClosedAt' = next
--- REPLACE
    /\ hoOpen' = FALSE
\* MUTATION: the heads may be understated.
    /\ \E h \in 0..next : hoClosedAt' = h
--- END
